3304"] ["question-bff2c616-f045-5186-8916-8acfc055fce7" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvector corresponding to the only eigenvalue of the system's matrix $A$ is $v=[1,\\text{ }0]^{T}.$ The vector $w=[0,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ is such that $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{{field-1}}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}{{field-2}},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the \n{{field-3}} \nSince ${e}^{4t}\\to $ \n{{field-4}} \nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move toward \n{{field-5}}  \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/27/27e921a76383c4f8a4fc1e81a1febcfad53f330d0e902f4e07578238da33422f.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={{field-6}} \\\\ y={e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.07$ | $0$ | {{field-7}} |\n| $y$ | $0.14$ | $1$ | {{field-8}} |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/36/36ae671944545eaae9027ef0d4a876e12ceef17d01be0ad881d32dfdcb8ad963.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/1f/1fd20f7333800323c44f41d7906958a0928d5f30279e36b1f50d0ca1f66fcd46.png)"] ["question-bff2c616-f045-5186-8916-8acfc055fce7" :question/worked-solution "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =4,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{4t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x\\text{-axis}.$ Since ${e}^{4t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move toward $\\text{infinity}$ in the phase plane as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/27/27e921a76383c4f8a4fc1e81a1febcfad53f330d0e902f4e07578238da33422f.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t{e}^{4t} \\\\ y={e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.07$ | $0$ | $1.98$ |\n| $y$ | $0.14$ | $1$ | $4.95$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/fd/fd431b8daf3ad9c1b25225af9d64b1e4876e4e1a90e1dfd010de8ed134ae323c.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/1f/1fd20f7333800323c44f41d7906958a0928d5f30279e36b1f50d0ca1f66fcd46.png)"] ["question-bff2c616-f045-5186-8916-8acfc055fce7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-bfb04862-ac9b-5f21-97c1-b9e7e940122c" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfb04862-ac9b-5f21-97c1-b9e7e940122c"] ["answer-a83cbb15-c2b0-51de-9c0d-a91b9bf42153" :answer/id #uuid "a83cbb15-c2b0-51de-9c0d-a91b9bf42153"] ["answer-a83cbb15-c2b0-51de-9c0d-a91b9bf42153" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a83cbb15-c2b0-51de-9c0d-a91b9bf42153" :answer/value "t{e}^{-4t}"] ["answer-0ad8aa71-7dcc-53a7-80cc-ee9c258321b7" :answer/id #uuid "0ad8aa71-7dcc-53a7-80cc-ee9c258321b7"] ["answer-0ad8aa71-7dcc-53a7-80cc-ee9c258321b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0ad8aa71-7dcc-53a7-80cc-ee9c258321b7" :answer/value "t{e}^{4t}"] ["answer-c8e9d164-6cbd-5d65-9cfb-1c7f1bc11422" :answer/id #uuid "c8e9d164-6cbd-5d65-9cfb-1c7f1bc11422"] ["answer-c8e9d164-6cbd-5d65-9cfb-1c7f1bc11422" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c8e9d164-6cbd-5d65-9cfb-1c7f1bc11422" :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}"] ["answer-dcf81baf-3c3b-5532-b109-a4a6a5ac3b60" :answer/id #uuid "dcf81baf-3c3b-5532-b109-a4a6a5ac3b60"] ["answer-dcf81baf-3c3b-5532-b109-a4a6a5ac3b60" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dcf81baf-3c3b-5532-b109-a4a6a5ac3b60" :answer/value "{e}^{4t}"] ["answer-field-bfb04862-ac9b-5f21-97c1-b9e7e940122c" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-bfb04862-ac9b-5f21-97c1-b9e7e940122c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-bfb04862-ac9b-5f21-97c1-b9e7e940122c" :answer-field/correct "answer-0ad8aa71-7dcc-53a7-80cc-ee9c258321b7"] ["answer-field-bfb04862-ac9b-5f21-97c1-b9e7e940122c" :answer-field/choices "answer-a83cbb15-c2b0-51de-9c0d-a91b9bf42153"] ["answer-field-bfb04862-ac9b-5f21-97c1-b9e7e940122c" :answer-field/choices "answer-0ad8aa71-7dcc-53a7-80cc-ee9c258321b7"] ["answer-field-bfb04862-ac9b-5f21-97c1-b9e7e940122c" :answer-field/choices "answer-c8e